  "videoHubTitle": "Watch & Listen",
  "videoHubSubtitle": "Animated educational videos in simple language",
  "videoEp1Title": "What are Stem Cells?",
  "videoEp1Desc": "Visual introduction to human stem cells, their self-renewal, and specialization.",
  "videoEp1Narration": "Stem cells are special cells in the human body that can renew themselves and develop into different types of specialized cells like blood, bone, and nerve cells. They act as our natural repair system.",
  "videoEp2Title": "Types of Stem Cells",
  "videoEp2Desc": "Explains Hematopoietic (HSC), Mesenchymal (MSC), and Cord Blood stem cells and their distinct medical roles.",
  "videoEp2Narration": "The two major clinical categories are Hematopoietic stem cells, which build your blood and immune system, and Mesenchymal stem cells, which form bone and cartilage. Newborn cord blood is an abundant source of young stem cells.",
  "videoEp3Title": "How Stem-Cell Therapy Works",
  "videoEp3Desc": "Step-by-step animation of conditioning chemotherapy, donor cell infusion, and the 21-day marrow engraftment process.",
  "videoEp3Narration": "Stem cell transplantation begins with conditioning therapy to clear non-functioning cells. Next, healthy stem cells are infused through a simple venous IV line. In two to three weeks, they engraft inside the marrow to produce healthy cells.",
  "videoEp4Title": "Cord Blood Collection & Biobanking",
  "videoEp4Desc": "How newborn umbilical cord blood is safely collected at birth with zero pain and preserved at -196°C in liquid nitrogen vapor.",
  "videoEp4Narration": "Directly after childbirth, leftover blood in the umbilical cord is collected painlessly for mother and child. It is tested and preserved in cryo-tanks at minus 196 degrees Celsius for future medical treatments.",
  "videoEp5Title": "Risks & Avoiding Unapproved Treatments",
  "videoEp5Desc": "Critical medical warnings from oncologists on identifying illegal clinics and false \"miracle cure\" advertisements.",
  "videoEp5Narration": "Beware of commercial spas claiming stem cells cure all chronic diseases, autism, or anti-aging. Legitimate therapies are regulated by ICMR and CDSCO and never promise unrealistic 100 percent miracle cures.",
